A||||9||jch82||My First Fiero!!!  Woohoo!!||||7||
Z||000000||jch82||04-02-2001||09:49 PM||||I finally got my first fiero!!! It is an 85GT, silver with grey ground effects. I bought it from a guy over in Saginaw, MI. <P>This was his ad in the Michigan Fiero Club Classifieds...<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>85 Silver Gt Runs But needs Work<BR>I have a 85 silver gt 4 speed its runs but has some rod clacking the body is decent to good but the front has suffered a run in with a trailer hitch its crackeds and the paint is messed up a new nose and she's good as new tho I will try to get some pictures to send the interiors needs headliner and seats the rest is all there and decent needs some electrical work to get stero and passanger side windows working I belive this is a heck of a car but I just cant afford to fix er up 600 obo you pick up She really has potential.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This had to have been the buy of the day because I get to his place and it looks to be in great shape. The front bumper can be glued back together and repainted. I figure the engine is junk because he says it has a bad knock in the rods.....I get in and drive it and it runs great! <P>There is some slight noise (in the engine) but I figure what the heck, for 450$ might as well buy it. He also said the clutch didn't engage right but I get it home and realize the clutch pedal arm is slightly bent because it is aluminum. <P>Anyways, I dolly the fiero home and decide to change the oil, oil filter and air filter(all were in rough shape). I take out the oil plug and only about a quart and a half of oil comes out....Filled her up with new oil and surprisingly NO MORE KNOCK. <P>Tomorrow I'm going to put on new pads and machine the rotors...Can't wait to get 'er all fixed up...I'll take some pics and post them in the next couple days.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Another thing I thought was wierd were the options it came with. It doesn't have a sunroof or spoiler (has a luggage rack). Has rear defrost, cruise, power windows/locks (not mirrors), speaker seats which are the factory grey/dark grey combo, and on the top of the ground effects when you open the door it says <I>Fisher Body</I> and it also says <I>Fiero[/i} on the little black inserts...Don't know if these are rare options to have but I thought it was pretty strange.<P>Josh   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 [i]-Blink 182</I><p>[This message has been edited by jch82 (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||MooCow||04-02-2001||09:54 PM||||Yea I went with and this guy had no clue what he had.  We have to fix my brakes there too josh.  A yeah congrats on your first and not last Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>                                  Thanks Ken<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||10
